The kanji is the question, and the card turns both ways

Front is the written word, back is how it reads and what it means.  Tapping
flips it either direction once she has seen the answer, so the three buttons
never disappear under her.

Adds the two bars she asked for - Learning, and Memorized for anything the
schedule has parked over a month or she has waved off - the round number for
the word on screen, a boards button on the card itself, and the crossed eye
that takes a word out of rotation.  The Known board is how it comes back.

